        Root cause:
        The bug was caused by an off-by-one error in the length checks for the backing file name in both the qcow and qcow2 implementations. The original checks did not account for the null terminator (`'\0'`), allowing for a potential buffer overflow when the backing file name reached the maximum allowed length. This oversight could lead to memory corruption or application crashes when handling backing file names that are at or near the maximum size.

